    "objective": "Implement the deterministic topological ordering helper used by ledger work-packet planning, to the contract and interface declared on this packet.",
    "contract": "Implement exactly this public function:\n\n    topological_order(graph: dict[str, list[str]]) -> list[str]\n\n    The graph maps each node to its list of SUCCESSOR nodes (edge node ->\n    successor). Return every node exactly once, including nodes that appear only\n    as successors and nodes with no edges. At each step choose the\n    alphabetically smallest node that is currently ready: every predecessor must\n    already be placed. Ignore duplicate edges. Raise ValueError for a cycle,\n    including a self-loop. Return [] for an empty graph. Do not mutate graph.\n\n    Use only the standard library. No placeholders or TODOs. Write the complete\n    module with the function and any private helpers it needs.",
    "interface": [
      "graph | required | dict[str, list[str]] -- directed graph mapping each node to successors"
    ],
    "interface_digest": "fac6d37529c6b3ce",
    "acceptance_criteria": [
      "every key and successor-only node appears exactly once",
      "each edge points from an earlier node to a later node",
      "the alphabetically smallest currently-ready node is selected",
      "duplicate edges are ignored and cycles raise ValueError",
      "empty input returns [] and the input is not mutated"
    ],
    "write_scope": [
      "src/topo_sort.py"
    ],
